      "name": "Soil property disclosure",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "soil-property",
      "description": "A report row preserves unavailable data; native disclosure remains operable.",
      "html": "<details class=\"ds-property\"><summary><span>Soil pH in water</span><strong>— <small>unavailable</small></strong></summary><p>Source unavailable. Regional map estimates are separate from laboratory measurements.</p></details>",
      "css": ".ds-property{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#e4e9e6);padding:12px 0;color:var(--ink,#18221e)}.ds-property summary{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;cursor:pointer;gap:12px;font-size:13px;list-style:none}.ds-property summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.ds-property summary>span{max-width:58%}.ds-property summary>span::after{content:\" +\";color:var(--muted,#59665f)}.ds-property[open] summary>span::after{content:\" −\"}.ds-property strong{font-size:20px;font-weight:500;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-property small{font-size:11px;font-weight:400;color:var(--muted,#59665f)}.ds-property p{font-size:12px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted,#59665f)}.ds-property summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#126a82);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:540px){.ds-property summary{font-size:14px;min-height:30px}.ds-property p{font-size:13px}.ds-property small{font-size:12px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Wetness legend",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Surface, root-zone and explicit missing-value encodings.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-wetness-key\"><span>Surface</span><span>Root zone</span><span class=\"ds-missing\">Missing</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-wetness-key{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;display:flex;gap:20px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted,#59665f)}.ds-wetness-key span::before{content:\"\";display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;background:var(--accent,#246c61);margin-right:6px}.ds-wetness-key span+span::before{background:#bdc9c0}.ds-wetness-key .ds-missing::before{background:transparent;border:1px dashed #8b9e91}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Historical measurement method",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Native disclosure keeps extraction methods and empty observations explicit.",
      "html": "<details class=\"ds-lab\"><summary><span>Extractable phosphorus — Olsen</span><strong>0 compatible records</strong></summary><p>No compatible CC-BY observations were returned for this region and depth. This is a data gap, not a zero concentration.</p></details>",
      "css": ".ds-lab{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#e4e9e6);color:var(--ink,#18221e)}.ds-lab summary{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;cursor:pointer;gap:20px;font-size:14px}.ds-lab summary>strong{font-size:12px;font-weight:400;color:var(--muted,#59665f)}.ds-lab p{color:var(--muted,#59665f);font-size:13px;line-height:1.7}.ds-lab summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#126a82);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:540px){.ds-lab summary{align-items:start;flex-direction:column;gap:6px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Planning: Primary button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-primary",
      "description": "Retained ?workspace=planning only. Filled replay action.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-primary\">Replay seasons</button>",
      "css": ".ds-primary{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;border:1px solid #cdd6d0;border-radius:6px;padding:9px 13px;min-height:38px;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;background:var(--ink,#18221e);border-color:var(--ink,#18221e);color:var(--surface,#fff)}.ds-primary:hover{background:#32453a}.ds-primary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus,#126a82);outline-offset:4px}.ds-primary:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:wait}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Planning: Plan panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "plan-panel",
      "description": "Retained ?workspace=planning only. Flat grouping surface for editable calendar information.",
      "html": "<fieldset class=\"ds-panel\"><legend class=\"ds-panel-title\">June planting</legend><p class=\"ds-panel-copy\">Starts at sowing. Default 55 / 30 / 30 days is illustrative; use locally reviewed stages.</p></fieldset>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;min-width:0;border:0;background:var(--raised,#f6f8f7);padding:17px 20px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin:0;color:var(--ink,#18221e)}.ds-panel-title{float:left;width:100%;font-size:16px;font-weight:500;margin-bottom:16px;padding:0}.ds-panel-copy{clear:both;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted,#59665f);margin:0}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Planning: Proportional calendar strip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "calendar-strip",
      "description": "Retained ?workspace=planning only. Three crop stages weighted by duration with explicit labels.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-calendar\" aria-label=\"Vegetative 55 days, Reproductive 30 days, Ripening 30 days\"><span class=\"ds-stage-a\">55d</span><span class=\"ds-stage-b\">30d</span><span class=\"ds-stage-c\">30d</span></div><div class=\"ds-stage-legend\"><span>Vegetative</span><span>Reproductive</span><span>Ripening</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-calendar{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;display:flex;gap:3px;height:25px;border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden}.ds-calendar span{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:11px;color:#193d32}.ds-stage-a{flex:55;background:#d4e3db}.ds-stage-b{flex:30;background:#89b3a1}.ds-stage-c{flex:30;background:#e3e9df}.ds-stage-legend{font-family:\"IBM Plex Sans\",sans-serif;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;color:var(--muted,#59665f);font-size:11px;margin:5px 0 13px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Regional Evidence Sheet",
    "overview": "A green-grey workspace frames a white evidence sheet. Quiet ink, restrained teal and self-hosted IBM Plex Sans preserve TerraProof's working character while natural Earth imagery gives geographic context. The default entry is a globe beside region controls and a soil report, with the selected rectangle as the working object.\n\nThe journey is global globe → region → evidence-backed soil profile. Regional SoilGrids predictions, NASA wetness at the centroid and historical WoSIS point observations remain visually separate. Values carry their units, source scale, coverage and limits; the interface offers neither pinpoint diagnosis nor a universal soil-quality grade. The earlier paired-calendar interface remains a secondary workspace at `?workspace=planning`, available only when the host allows private planning.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Green-grey frame and white evidence sheet.",
      "Interactive Earth with a restrained teal region overlay.",
      "Flat report rows, fine separators and explicit units.",
      "Regional predictions, centroid context and historical measurements presented separately.",
      "Globe-first mobile stacking and keyboard coordinate entry.",
      "Retained calendar planning patterns scoped to the secondary workspace."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Evidence Label Rule",
        "body": "Keep property units, series names, region bounds and source scale alongside color; color alone does not explain a result.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Regional Evidence Rule",
        "body": "Spatial P10–P90 describes variation across sampled map predictions, not confidence intervals or field accuracy. Do not present regional medians as pinpoint soil diagnoses. Total nitrogen is not plant-available nitrogen; carbon concentration is not organic matter percentage; CEC is not available N/P/K.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the green-grey frame, white sheet, IBM Plex Sans and quiet teal across both workspaces.",
      "Do lead the default entry with the globe and selected-region report; scope the sidebar and calendars to planning.",
      "Do keep regional map predictions, NASA centroid wetness and historical WoSIS observations separate.",
      "Do retain source scale, sampled coverage, missing values, assessed bounds and stale-result notices.",
      "Do use self-hosted IBM Plex Sans and tabular numbers for the working interface.",
      "Do retain plan names, units and exact-value tables alongside chart colors.",
      "Do keep keyboard focus visible and scrollable evidence regions named and focusable.",
      "Do retain the mobile horizontal-scroll cue beside the stage evidence table.",
      "Do keep source limits and the distinction between exposure and economics visible."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't claim field accuracy percentages, confidence intervals from spatial P10–P90, pinpoint diagnoses or a universal soil-quality score.",
      "Don't imply the Blue Marble reference imagery is live or that historical WoSIS samples validate current regional predictions.",
      "Don't add shadows or decorative gradients to the existing panel hierarchy.",
      "Don't encode a winning plan or predicted crop damage through the comparison palette.",
      "Don't shrink wide evidence tables until their units and dates become unreadable.",
      "Don't replace visible field labels with placeholder-only controls.",
      "Don't add motion that ignores the existing reduced-motion preference."
    ]
  }
}
